{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:1", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Even if sin were piled high as a mountain many yojanas wide, it is destroyed by the yoga of meditation, and by nothing else ever.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:101-105", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "101-105"}, "paraphrase": "When the nāda is heard and the Self is seen in the cavity of the skull, the yogin attains kaivalya.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:nada"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:14", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "14"}, "paraphrase": "Oṃ is the bow, the self the arrow, Brahman the target; it is to be pierced by the heedful (quoting Muṇḍaka).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "practices": ["prc:pranava-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:19-21", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "19-21"}, "paraphrase": "Meditate on Oṃ as the thumb-sized Lord in the heart; Brahmā is inhalation, Viṣṇu retention, Rudra exhalation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "practices": ["prc:pranava-dhyana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:41-43", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "41-43"}, "paraphrase": "Posture, breath-restraint, withdrawal, concentration, meditation and absorption are the six limbs. There are as many postures as beings; four are named — siddha, bhadra, siṃha and padma.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "paths": ["pth:dhyanabindu-six-limbs"], "practices": ["prc:asanas-yoga-upanisads"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:43-54", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "43-54"}, "paraphrase": "The body's centres: the ādhāra with four petals and the triangle (yoni) and liṅga; the svādhiṣṭhāna; the maṇipūra, a twelve-spoked wheel where the jīva wanders driven by merit and sin; the kanda from which 72,000 channels spread, ten of them principal (iḍā, piṅgalā, suṣumnā, gāndhārī, hastijihvā, pūṣā, yaśasvinī, alambusā, kuhū, śaṅkhinī).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:cakras", "cpt:nadis"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:58-60", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "58-60"}, "paraphrase": "The jīva, moved by prāṇa and apāna, goes up and down, never resting, like a ball struck by the hand, or a bird tied by a string that flies off and is pulled back.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-vayus"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:61-65", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "61-65"}, "paraphrase": "The jīva goes out with the sound ha and returns with sa, repeating 'haṃsa' 21,600 times a day; this ajapā-gāyatrī gives liberation to yogins; knowing it one is freed from sin.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:ajapa-gayatri", "cpt:hamsa"], "practices": ["prc:ajapa-japa"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:66-68", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "66-68"}, "paraphrase": "The kuṇḍalinī sleeps covering with her mouth the door to Brahman; awakened by fire, mind and breath, she rises through the suṣumnā like a needle drawing thread; the yogin opens the door of liberation with her as a key opens a door.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:kundalini"], "practices": ["prc:sakticalana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:79-92-summary", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "79-92 (summary)"}, "paraphrase": "Khecarī mudrā and the retention of bindu are described: bindu is twofold, white (śukla, Śiva) and red (rajas, Śakti), and their union in the body is the yogin's aim. Recorded as a summary only.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "body-layers"], "practices": ["prc:khecari-mudra"], "concepts": ["cpt:bindu"], "restricted": true, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:9-12", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "9-12"}, "paraphrase": "Oṃ's letters correspond to Vedas, worlds and deities; a is yellow and of rajas, u white and of sattva, m black and of tamas.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:omkara-matras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:93-94-petal-moods", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "93-94 (petal moods)"}, "paraphrase": "In the heart lotus the moods follow the petals: east (white) dharma, south-east (red) sleep and sloth, south (black) hatred, south-west (blue) sin and violence, west (crystal) play, north-west (ruby) going and dispassion, north (yellow) pleasure, north-east (lapis) charity; at the junctions, disease; at the centre, knowing all.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:heart-lotus-petals"], "cross_refs": ["tea:hamsa-upanisad:3-heart-lotus"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dhyanabindu-upanisad:94-five-states", "source": "src:dhyanabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "94 (five states)"}, "paraphrase": "Resting in the successive circles of the lotus the self experiences waking, dream, deep sleep, the fourth and what is beyond the fourth.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:turiya-turiyatita"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
